{{also|Peptide}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From {{bor|en|de|Peptid}}, from {{der|en|grc|πεπτός||digested}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈpɛptaɪd/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-peptide.wav|Audio (UK)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|organic compound}} Any of a [[class]] of [[organic]] [[compound]]s consisting of various numbers of [[amino acid]]s in which the [[amine]] of one is reacted with the [[carboxylic acid]] of the next to form an [[amide]] bond.
#* {{quote-book
|en
|title=On Food and Cooking: The Science and Lore of the Kitchen
|author=Harold McGee
|authorlink=Harold McGee
|year=2004
|publisher=Scribner
|isbn=978-0-684-80001-1
|chapter=1
|passage=When it’s digested, its long amino-acid chains are first broken down into smaller fragments, or '''peptides'''. It turns out that many hormones and drugs are also '''peptides''', and a number of casein '''peptides''' do affect the body in hormone-like ways.}}
# {{lb|en|chemistry}} The [[peptide bond]] itself.

